<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">patch</ansi>

When a battle ends, your company's healers patch everyone up on their own:

  <ansi fg="command">Your company patches itself up.</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">Brother Oswin heals Garrick Vane: 13 health.</ansi>

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How it works</ansi>

- Every member with you who knows <ansi fg="yellow">Minor Heal</ansi> heals, the one with the most
  mana to spare first, the most hurt member first.
- Each member is healed up to your company's <ansi fg="yellow">healing threshold</ansi> (50% of
  their wound limit unless you change it; <ansi fg="command">help tactics</ansi>), and no
  further. Someone bleeding out is healed too.
- Each heal costs the usual mana (3) and heals the usual amount: 10 to 16
  health, plus 1 for every 6 levels of the healer, 5% more with a holy
  symbol.
- A healer stops at its <ansi fg="yellow">mana reserve</ansi> (<ansi fg="command">strategy [who] reserve [percent]</ansi>,
  <ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>), so it keeps that share for the next battle.
- Only heals: no wounds are tended, no bandages or splints used, and only
  your own company is healed, never an allied player's.
- It takes no game time. If a waiting group starts the next battle at
  once, there is no time to patch.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">On demand</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">company patch</ansi>    (or just <ansi fg="command">patch</ansi>) runs the same healing now

It can't be used in a battle, while travelling, or while resting. For a
full tending that goes past the threshold, uses bandages and splints and
spends every drop of mana, use <ansi fg="command">heal wounds</ansi> (<ansi fg="command">help heal</ansi>).

Mana doesn't come back on its own: when your healers run dry, rest in a
camp or an inn, or drink a mana draught (<ansi fg="command">help mana</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help draughts</ansi>).

See also: <ansi fg="command">help heal</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help tactics</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help wounds</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.
